# Claude Code per-developer overrides (the committed .claude/settings.json is
# the team baseline; .claude/settings.local.json is for personal permissions
# and tweaks that should never reach the repo). The un-ignore is required
# because the broader `*.json` rule above otherwise excludes settings.json.
!.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Backup files
*.bak
*.backup
*~

# Meeting transcripts (auto-generated by meeting tools, contain raw speaker IDs
# and may include sensitive context; keep local-only — the formal acta lives in
# .planning/phases/<phase>/MEETING-*-NOTES.md).
reintentos.txt
*-transcript.txt

# Production logs pulled from the server for local analysis. May contain
# payment info, CFDI UUIDs, PO numbers and other customer data — keep
# local-only, never commit.
data/

# Artefacto de `npm test`: la suite PaymentReconciliation llama a CsvWriter, que
# resuelve su ruta relativa al CWD, así que en local aterriza en la raíz del repo
# en vez de C:\Logs\sageconnect\<fecha>\. El contenido es sintético (PY-001,
# portal-1, 1000 MXN) pero el archivo APPENDEA entre corridas y nada lo trunca.
# Esto es la mitad barata de 20.4 D-ITEM-01; la honesta es que la suite escriba a
# un directorio temporal y limpie, como ya hace tests/config.probe-budget.test.js.
/sageconnect/
